00:02:20.090 --> 00:02:21.760
Now back to the show.

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:23.900
First, a quick primer on the show.

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:25.680
And yeah, try to keep up.

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:28.090
Season one introduces us to David Haller.

00:02:28.090 --> 00:02:30.980
Who his whole life has
been told that he's insane.

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:33.230
But after being rescued
from the governments grasp,

00:02:33.230 --> 00:02:35.060
by a group of like minded mutants.

00:02:35.060 --> 00:02:37.800
David learns that he
actually has psychic powers.

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:40.000
And begins training to control his power.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:43.420
The only problem is that a
powerful telepath, Amahl Farouk,

00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:46.340
has been lodged in his
brain since he was a baby.

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:48.510
And is now is trying
to take over his mind.

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:50.630
Well season one ends with
Farouk being kicked out

00:02:50.630 --> 00:02:51.610
of David's brain.

00:02:51.610 --> 00:02:54.610
Season two focuses on the
group trying to kill him.

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:56.550
Except not really, because
we learn that David

00:02:56.550 --> 00:02:58.510
is actually kind of an evil asshole.

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:00.730
Not above torturing a
friend to get what he wants

00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:03.030
or raping his girlfriend Sydney Barrett.

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:05.380
In one of televisions
biggest bait and switches,

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:07.820
season two ends with the
group befriending Farouk,

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:08.990
and hunting David.

00:03:08.990 --> 00:03:11.370
Fast forward a few months,
where season three picks up.

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:13.450
David has decided to live a quiet life

00:03:13.450 --> 00:03:16.877
as a cult leader for young
women with abandonment issues.

00:03:16.877 --> 00:03:17.773
- We?

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:19.929
- [David] My people.

00:03:19.929 --> 00:03:21.342
- Your commune?

00:03:21.342 --> 00:03:22.540
Are you talking about your commune,

00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:25.270
where you seduce teenage
girls with daddy issues?

00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:27.040
- [Michael] That is
until the time traveler,

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:28.350
Switch, arrives.

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:30.560
But David's not interested
in going back in time

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:31.670
and righting his wrong.

00:03:31.670 --> 00:03:34.300
Instead, he wants to
go so far back in time,

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:35.680
that he stops Amhal Farouk

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:38.260
from ever inhabiting his
brain in the first place.

00:03:38.260 --> 00:03:40.230
In the process stopping all the literal

00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:41.910
madness that has occurred since.

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:44.160
The only problem is that Switch's powers

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:45.730
aren't fully developed yet.

00:03:45.730 --> 00:03:47.480
And by going so far back in time,

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:51.240
David has angered some
seriously creepy baddies.

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:54.541
- In the hall of time, there are demons.

00:03:54.541 --> 00:03:57.150
- Wait, demons?

00:03:57.150 --> 00:03:59.180
- [Michael] Still, David
and Switch keep at it,

00:03:59.180 --> 00:04:01.490
which causes some disastrous consequences

00:04:01.490 --> 00:04:03.010
for the present, like, oh right,

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:04.655
potentially ending the world.

00:04:04.655 --> 00:04:06.070
- This is how he does it.

00:04:06.070 --> 00:04:07.040
- [Michael] While Sydney and the others

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:08.750
race backwards in time to stop David

00:04:08.750 --> 00:04:10.150
from doing anymore damage,

00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:12.460
David meets up with
his father in the past.

00:04:12.460 --> 00:04:14.840
Telepath, Charles Xavier of X Men fame.

00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:16.780
And teams up with him to kill Farouk.

00:04:16.780 --> 00:04:18.640
Except future Farouk joins the mix,

00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:21.820
and convinces Charles that
violence isn't the answer.

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:23.710
After one touching father son moment,

00:04:23.710 --> 00:04:25.950
and a slightly less
touching, but still moving

00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:27.550
past future Farouk moment,

00:04:27.550 --> 00:04:29.560
everyone comes to an understanding.

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:31.380
- I'm saying that war is not the answer,

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:35.020
it's the problem, David we
don't need this barbarism,

00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:36.470
I've made a deal with Farouk.

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:38.950
- Are you saying we just leave?

00:04:38.950 --> 00:04:40.510
- I'm saying that we respect their right

00:04:40.510 --> 00:04:42.900
to exist and they respect ours, yours.

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:44.950
- With the past successfully changed,

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:47.310
David and Sydney look over
the crib at baby David,

00:04:47.310 --> 00:04:49.740
before they both disappear into the ether.

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:54.350
Having effectively erased their
own existences, and scene.

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:56.090
Now if all of that doesn't seem

00:04:56.090 --> 00:04:58.490
perfectly clear to you, don't panic.

00:04:58.490 --> 00:04:59.450
From the get go,

00:04:59.450 --> 00:05:01.190
Legion has always been about challenging

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:02.610
the audiences expectations,

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:04.470
and season three is no different.

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:06.680
Simply put, it's confusing.

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:07.710
What does it all mean?

00:05:07.710 --> 00:05:10.590
Well, here's our two best takes.

00:05:10.590 --> 00:05:13.870
Idea One: Metaphor &amp; Metaphysics.

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:16.020
In case it wasn't immediately obvious,

00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:19.010
Legion thrives on an
ambiguous sense of reality.

00:05:19.010 --> 00:05:20.260
Throughout the shows three seasons,

00:05:20.260 --> 00:05:22.070
we are constantly asking ourselves,

00:05:22.070 --> 00:05:23.590
what is real or true?

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:25.250
Is David Haller really David,

00:05:25.250 --> 00:05:28.503
or is he the host of other
personalities inside his head?

00:05:28.503 --> 00:05:30.300
- Who the hell are you?

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:31.163
- I am Legion.

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:35.010
- I am Legion

00:05:35.010 --> 00:05:36.430
- [Michael] Is Amhal Farouk really evil?

00:05:36.430 --> 00:05:38.710
Or is he actually a
loving surrogate father?

00:05:38.710 --> 00:05:40.810
- I love the boy Charles.

00:05:40.810 --> 00:05:43.100
- As it turns out, much of this ambiguity

00:05:43.100 --> 00:05:46.390
stems from the shows
unabashed love for metaphors.

00:05:46.390 --> 00:05:47.830
But when we say metaphor,

00:05:47.830 --> 00:05:51.080
we're not just talking about
simply comparing two things.

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:54.460
But a very specific
philosophical sense of the word.

00:05:54.460 --> 00:05:57.210
Borrowing from the work of
philosopher Richard Moran,

00:05:57.210 --> 00:05:58.080
we can say that,

00:05:58.080 --> 00:06:00.340
Metaphors create a sense of Ambiguity

00:06:00.340 --> 00:06:02.910
because of the framing
effects they produce.

00:06:02.910 --> 00:06:04.910
In Moran's view, metaphors force people

00:06:04.910 --> 00:06:07.700
to consider and object or
situation in a new light,

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:09.550
by contrasting it with another.

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:13.090
Importantly, this framing
isn't fixed nor is its meaning.

00:06:13.090 --> 00:06:15.520
And this is where our ambiguity creeps in.

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:17.303
When the show calls Farouk
a monster for example,

00:06:17.303 --> 00:06:18.770
this could mean anything,

00:06:18.770 --> 00:06:21.740
from the fact that he's
technically an alien life form,

00:06:21.740 --> 00:06:23.720
to the fact that he's incredibly powerful,

00:06:23.720 --> 00:06:25.810
to the fact that he once
trapped a king's mind

00:06:25.810 --> 00:06:27.630
inside that of a monkeys.

00:06:27.630 --> 00:06:31.740
- By monster, you mean
like a metaphor, right?

00:06:31.740 --> 00:06:33.960
- As philosopher Donald
Davidson points out.

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:36.730
Most metaphors don't
possess definite meanings

00:06:36.730 --> 00:06:38.070
anymore than dreams do.

00:06:38.070 --> 00:06:41.260
After all, when Romeo
compares Juliet to the sun,

00:06:41.260 --> 00:06:44.180
there are a million and one
different things it could mean.

00:06:44.180 --> 00:06:45.870
In the same way that dreaming you're naked

00:06:45.870 --> 00:06:47.110
in front of your high school class

00:06:47.110 --> 00:06:49.240
could mean both everything, and nothing.

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:52.630
But what's important here is
by framing Juliet with the sun,

00:06:52.630 --> 00:06:55.550
we're creating an infinite
amount of associations.

00:06:55.550 --> 00:06:57.900
According to Davidson,
just like in dreams,

00:06:57.900 --> 00:07:00.280
a metaphor's meaning is interpretive.

00:07:00.280 --> 00:07:03.090
At its best, the dream like
logic behind metaphors,

00:07:03.090 --> 00:07:04.220
really does drive home,

00:07:04.220 --> 00:07:07.070
how ambiguous Legion's reality really is.

00:07:07.070 --> 00:07:09.410
Take season two, in which
episodes often begin

00:07:09.410 --> 00:07:10.860
with an educational segment

00:07:10.860 --> 00:07:13.500
that later contextualizes
the action on screen.

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:16.803
- [Narrator] Psychologists
call it a conversion disorder.

00:07:20.170 --> 00:07:22.850
In that the body converts a mental stress

00:07:23.890 --> 00:07:26.320
to a set of physical symptoms,

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:28.713
in this case, a tick or spasm.

00:07:31.430 --> 00:07:36.250
And like any disorder
it can be contagious.

00:07:37.660 --> 00:07:39.770
- At first these segments
seem to contextualize

00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:42.560
our understanding of the
various telepathic phenomenon

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:43.710
going on in the show.

00:07:43.710 --> 00:07:46.503
The spread of our teeth
clacking zombies, for example.

00:07:46.503 --> 00:07:48.040
(teeth clacking)

00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:49.870
Is compared to the way
conversion disorders

00:07:49.870 --> 00:07:51.630
like laughing fits and mass hysterics

00:07:51.630 --> 00:07:53.120
have spread throughout history.

00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:54.180
In another segment,

00:07:54.180 --> 00:07:56.810
delusions are characterized
like parasites,

00:07:56.810 --> 00:08:00.480
feeding on rational ideas,
until only they are left.

00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:03.530
This in turn, later explains
the spread of delusion

00:08:03.530 --> 00:08:05.350
among the members of division three.

00:08:05.350 --> 00:08:07.410
That an admiral must be killed.

00:08:07.410 --> 00:08:09.050
- I'll have our rumors, whisperers,

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:11.260
people go to Admiral Fukuyama's pedestal.

00:08:11.260 --> 00:08:12.480
And they don't come back.

00:08:12.480 --> 00:08:13.530
- What does he do to them?

00:08:13.530 --> 00:08:14.906
- He eats them.

00:08:14.906 --> 00:08:18.080
- [Speaker System] System Alert.

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:19.630
- It's not gonna happen to us.

00:08:19.630 --> 00:08:22.330
- In both cases these
metaphors seem to contain

00:08:22.330 --> 00:08:23.850
fairly simple meanings.

00:08:23.850 --> 00:08:27.237
Madness is contagious and
delusion is destructive.

00:08:27.237 --> 00:08:31.000
But of course, meaning is a
moving target with metaphors.

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:32.930
And reality is constantly shifting

00:08:32.930 --> 00:08:34.320
under your feet in Legion.

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:36.670
While we spend a whole
season thinking we understand

00:08:36.670 --> 00:08:37.940
what these metaphors mean,

00:08:37.940 --> 00:08:39.690
the last episode of season two,

00:08:39.690 --> 00:08:42.750
really rips the rug from
underneath our collective feet.

00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:44.720
The madness that had been spreading,

00:08:44.720 --> 00:08:46.800
the delusion that had been growing.

00:08:46.800 --> 00:08:50.040
It was David, and boy, were we wrong.

00:08:50.040 --> 00:08:52.700
- David Haller, your
treachery has been discovered,

00:08:52.700 --> 00:08:54.880
the inevitability of your future crimes.

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:56.650
- [Michael] However, while
the end of season two

00:08:56.650 --> 00:08:58.210
might have been a high point for Legion's

00:08:58.210 --> 00:08:59.650
thematic use of metaphors.

00:08:59.650 --> 00:09:01.410
Season three demonstrates how sometimes

00:09:01.410 --> 00:09:04.170
the show can collapse
under a metaphors weight.

00:09:04.170 --> 00:09:05.390
Because lets be real here,

00:09:05.390 --> 00:09:08.940
some metaphors like dreams,
make zero sense at all.

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:10.410
I think the best example of this would be

00:09:10.410 --> 00:09:13.200
season three's depiction
of the astral plane.

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:15.860
As if it was purposefully
designed to give us a headache.

00:09:15.860 --> 00:09:19.562
The astral plane is both a
literal and metaphorical place.

00:09:19.562 --> 00:09:21.140
Amhal Farouk at one point gives us

00:09:21.140 --> 00:09:23.070
this no nonsense definition of it,

00:09:23.070 --> 00:09:24.933
well at least by Legions standards.

00:09:24.933 --> 00:09:29.933
- This is the astral plane,
a world beyond the world.

00:09:30.680 --> 00:09:32.107
Made of pure energy.

00:09:33.145 --> 00:09:35.917
Very few can see it.

00:09:35.917 --> 00:09:39.100
- [Michael] Meanwhile
Jermaine, I mean Oliver,

00:09:39.100 --> 00:09:40.730
tells us that the astral plane

00:09:40.730 --> 00:09:43.310
is kinda like the island of misfit toys.

00:09:43.310 --> 00:09:45.240
Where broken minds, forgotten truths

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:47.580
and lost objects all collect.

00:09:47.580 --> 00:09:49.453
- We were always finding things.

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:56.583
Pins, poetry, socks.

00:09:58.980 --> 00:10:01.530
The astral plane was like
a magnet for lost dreams.

00:10:08.310 --> 00:10:11.303
Minds, that was the other thing we found.

00:10:12.520 --> 00:10:16.000
In the real world, when
people lost their minds,

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:17.420
they ended up here.

00:10:17.420 --> 00:10:18.410
- On the surface,

00:10:18.410 --> 00:10:20.530
we're presented with
an interesting problem.

00:10:20.530 --> 00:10:22.530
How can a metaphorical place,

00:10:22.530 --> 00:10:24.530
where literal lost dreams come true,

00:10:24.530 --> 00:10:26.652
also be a real place?

00:10:26.652 --> 00:10:28.070
And what does this tell us

00:10:28.070 --> 00:10:30.670
about the larger logic motivating Legion?

00:10:30.670 --> 00:10:32.800
Well one way we could go
about this is to assume

00:10:32.800 --> 00:10:35.140
that both the physical
and mental properties

00:10:35.140 --> 00:10:37.210
are equally real in the show.

00:10:37.210 --> 00:10:39.630
If thoughts and matter all contain some,

00:10:39.630 --> 00:10:42.440
for lack of a better word, mental stuff,

00:10:42.440 --> 00:10:44.180
then it goes a long way in explaining

00:10:44.180 --> 00:10:46.670
how a metaphorical world
like the astral plane,

00:10:46.670 --> 00:10:49.470
can double as a real physical place.

00:10:49.470 --> 00:10:51.100
So, for example, while we might

00:10:51.100 --> 00:10:54.380
usually think of being
heartbroken as an emotional state,

00:10:54.380 --> 00:10:55.740
in the astral plane,

00:10:55.740 --> 00:10:57.580
you could literally find the embodiment

00:10:57.580 --> 00:11:00.180
of your broken heart,
bleeding out in the street.

00:11:00.180 --> 00:11:01.540
- Don't forget your heart.

00:11:01.540 --> 00:11:02.700
- [Michael] By having these mental states

00:11:02.700 --> 00:11:05.520
manifest themselves physically
in the astral plane,

00:11:05.520 --> 00:11:06.970
the show seems to be advocating

00:11:06.970 --> 00:11:09.230
for a sort of panpsychic doctrine.

00:11:09.230 --> 00:11:11.260
Distilled into its most basic component,

00:11:11.260 --> 00:11:13.870
panpsychism holds at
the old Cartesian divide

00:11:13.870 --> 00:11:17.250
between mind and body, isn't
really a divide at all.

00:11:17.250 --> 00:11:19.680
Instead, the pansychist
believes that everything

00:11:19.680 --> 00:11:21.530
from the glass in your smart phone,

00:11:21.530 --> 00:11:23.130
to the neurons in your brain,

00:11:23.130 --> 00:11:25.784
contains fundamental mental elements.

00:11:25.784 --> 00:11:27.590
Now before you start worrying that

00:11:27.590 --> 00:11:29.958
the ground beneath your feet has feelings.

00:11:29.958 --> 00:11:32.291
(squealing)

00:11:35.400 --> 00:11:37.880
- Pansychists usually
don't commit to the idea

00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:39.500
that everything has thoughts.

00:11:39.500 --> 00:11:41.360
Instead, most believe that everything

00:11:41.360 --> 00:11:43.330
has a mental experience.

00:11:43.330 --> 00:11:46.240
The mental experience of a
human might be quite complex,

00:11:46.240 --> 00:11:48.240
while that of a fly might be much simpler,

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:50.820
and that of a rock would
be even more basic.

00:11:50.820 --> 00:11:53.450
To most panpsychists, mental experience

00:11:53.450 --> 00:11:56.040
is a fundamental building
block of the universe.

00:11:56.040 --> 00:11:58.690
With actual thought only being achieved

00:11:58.690 --> 00:12:01.140
by sufficiently complex entities.

00:12:01.140 --> 00:12:02.700
Applying this model to Legion,

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:04.820
we can see how both
regular everyday objects

00:12:04.820 --> 00:12:07.140
and abstract ideas, like
the loss of innocence,

00:12:07.140 --> 00:12:08.920
appear in the astral plane.

00:12:08.920 --> 00:12:11.550
They all have a mental experience.

00:12:11.550 --> 00:12:14.200
It also goes a long way in
explaining why David struggles

00:12:14.200 --> 00:12:16.740
to differentiate between
his mind and reality.

00:12:16.740 --> 00:12:19.780
They're all made of the
same mental building blocks.

00:12:19.780 --> 00:12:24.780
- His mind is fixed, his
reality is alternate.

00:12:25.130 --> 00:12:26.350
- [Michael] But while
this is an interesting

00:12:26.350 --> 00:12:27.490
hook into the show,

00:12:27.490 --> 00:12:30.440
it's hard to say if the show
is really using panpsychism

00:12:30.440 --> 00:12:32.590
or metaphors to make any deeper arguments

00:12:32.590 --> 00:12:34.850
about the nature of reality or experience.

00:12:34.850 --> 00:12:36.230
When it comes to panpsychism,

00:12:36.230 --> 00:12:38.400
the show never seems to really draw out

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:41.440
any of the implications of
having reality and your mind

00:12:41.440 --> 00:12:43.040
being both equally real.

00:12:43.040 --> 00:12:44.910
Especially in regards to David.

00:12:44.910 --> 00:12:46.150
And when it comes to metaphor,

00:12:46.150 --> 00:12:48.280
it sometimes feels like
the show is confusing

00:12:48.280 --> 00:12:50.210
for the sake of being confusing.

00:12:50.210 --> 00:12:52.650
Sure, in an over saturated
superhero market,

00:12:52.650 --> 00:12:55.700
it might be fun to see musical
numbers stand in for dialog.

00:12:55.700 --> 00:12:57.500
- There's only one way this can end,

00:13:00.898 --> 00:13:02.770
a rap battle.

00:13:02.770 --> 00:13:04.570
- [Michael] But sometimes
we like to understand

00:13:04.570 --> 00:13:05.920
the literal narrative.

00:13:05.920 --> 00:13:08.300
After all, according to
playwright and screenwriter

00:13:08.300 --> 00:13:10.630
David Mamet, the core of drama is about,

00:13:10.630 --> 00:13:13.860
finding previously
unsuspected meaning in chaos,

00:13:13.860 --> 00:13:16.970
the truth that had been
previously obscured by lies.

00:13:16.970 --> 00:13:18.190
But maybe we should be okay

00:13:18.190 --> 00:13:20.390
with Legion's uneven use of metaphor.

00:13:20.390 --> 00:13:22.950
For a show that's so out there
in terms of art direction,

00:13:22.950 --> 00:13:24.700
maybe all the metaphors are just a way

00:13:24.700 --> 00:13:26.350
to tell an interesting story.

00:13:26.350 --> 00:13:28.010
Philosophy be damned.

00:13:28.010 --> 00:13:30.690
Going back to our philosophers
Moran and Davidson.

00:13:30.690 --> 00:13:33.340
Metaphors don't necessarily
have to make sense.

00:13:33.340 --> 00:13:35.150
The important thing is the effect.

00:13:35.150 --> 00:13:36.070
The framing.

00:13:36.070 --> 00:13:38.340
And effects seems to be Legions m.o.

00:13:38.340 --> 00:13:40.490
it's all about that style.

00:13:40.490 --> 00:13:43.130
So maybe we should forgive
the show for pelting us

00:13:43.130 --> 00:13:45.500
with various dance
numbers, loquacious asides.

00:13:45.500 --> 00:13:47.270
- It's about the order of things.

00:13:47.270 --> 00:13:51.430
The order you learn when you're
young, we let you be wild,

00:13:51.430 --> 00:13:52.930
because wildness is important,

00:13:54.380 --> 00:13:56.713
but as you grow older
we give you structure.

00:13:57.750 --> 00:13:58.890
So you'd feel safe.

00:13:58.890 --> 00:14:01.202
- [Michael] And the
very weird astral plane.

00:14:01.202 --> 00:14:04.186
♪ I'm the supine lupine
my libido kills sunshine ♪

00:14:04.186 --> 00:14:07.310
♪ Moody and spicy like a
fine ass toilet wine. ♪

00:14:07.310 --> 00:14:10.530
- Maybe all Legion is trying
to do is keep it interesting.

00:14:10.530 --> 00:14:12.849
So deep, maybe not.

00:14:12.849 --> 00:14:16.320
Idea Two: Time &amp; Change.

00:14:16.320 --> 00:14:18.880
Of course the big shake
up in season three,

00:14:18.880 --> 00:14:20.460
other than Ptonomy's mustache.

00:14:20.460 --> 00:14:22.710
Is the addition of the
time traveler, Switch.

00:14:22.710 --> 00:14:24.010
Now it might seem unfair

00:14:24.010 --> 00:14:25.860
to put Legion's depiction of time travel

00:14:25.860 --> 00:14:26.900
under the microscope.

00:14:26.900 --> 00:14:28.280
When it comes to comic book characters

00:14:28.280 --> 00:14:30.800
we kind of just have to
grant the initial premise.

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:32.840
Radioactive spiders giving you superpowers

00:14:32.840 --> 00:14:33.810
instead of cancer?

00:14:33.810 --> 00:14:35.410
Sure, why not.

00:14:35.410 --> 00:14:38.360
And early on, Legion playfully reminds us

00:14:38.360 --> 00:14:39.790
that its depiction of time travel

00:14:39.790 --> 00:14:42.350
isn't going to trey to heavily on science.

00:14:42.350 --> 00:14:44.730
- What do you know about time travel?

00:14:44.730 --> 00:14:46.620
- I have a PhD in quantum mechanics

00:14:46.620 --> 00:14:48.460
and a masters in nuclear physics.

00:14:48.460 --> 00:14:50.550
- Have you ever seen the hall?

00:14:50.550 --> 00:14:52.180
- The hall?

00:14:52.180 --> 00:14:56.170
- Time is a hallway, it
moves in two directions,

00:14:56.170 --> 00:14:58.140
forwards and back,

00:14:58.140 --> 00:15:03.123
and by drawing a doorway
in the air, like this,

00:15:04.480 --> 00:15:05.910
I can access the time stream.

00:15:05.910 --> 00:15:09.620
- But there has to be some
internal logic going on, right?

00:15:09.620 --> 00:15:12.350
Well in Legion's case, not really.

00:15:12.350 --> 00:15:14.960
In fact, the final season
continually fails to address

00:15:14.960 --> 00:15:17.970
one of the biggest logical
problems in time travel.

00:15:17.970 --> 00:15:19.530
The grandfather paradox.

00:15:19.530 --> 00:15:22.380
That is, how can time travel be possible

00:15:22.380 --> 00:15:23.400
if you went back in time,

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:25.490
killed your grandfather and
made sure you were never born

00:15:25.490 --> 00:15:27.790
to go back in time and
kill said grandfather.

00:15:27.790 --> 00:15:30.600
Now, there are a lot of
ways to tackle this problem.

00:15:30.600 --> 00:15:32.440
You could go the Marvel
route and just say,

00:15:32.440 --> 00:15:34.890
no matter what you do while
swanning around in the past

00:15:34.890 --> 00:15:36.260
the future doesn't change.

00:15:36.260 --> 00:15:38.453
- Time doesn't work that
way, changing the past

00:15:38.453 --> 00:15:40.190
doesn't change the future.

00:15:40.190 --> 00:15:41.990
- [Michael] As for Legion,
the show's solution

00:15:41.990 --> 00:15:44.470
can best be summed up as (bleep) it,

00:15:44.470 --> 00:15:45.460
come at me bro.

00:15:45.460 --> 00:15:48.377
(foreign language)

00:15:54.430 --> 00:15:56.870
- [Michael] Yeah, so
David does successfully

00:15:56.870 --> 00:15:59.030
change his past by keeping
his parents together

00:15:59.030 --> 00:16:01.190
and saving his baby
self from Amahl Farouk.

00:16:01.190 --> 00:16:05.700
In doing so, he literally
erases his current self.

00:16:05.700 --> 00:16:06.533
- So now what?

00:16:08.660 --> 00:16:10.037
We just sort of.

00:16:13.040 --> 00:16:16.770
- Fade away, into the ether.

00:16:16.770 --> 00:16:18.110
- How does this square with the fact,

00:16:18.110 --> 00:16:19.720
that if David hadn't shared his brain

00:16:19.720 --> 00:16:21.400
with Farouk for 33 years,

00:16:21.400 --> 00:16:23.760
he wouldn't have gone back
in time in the first place?

00:16:23.760 --> 00:16:24.770
It doesn't.

00:16:24.770 --> 00:16:26.320
But maybe Legion isn't trying

00:16:26.320 --> 00:16:28.530
to make a logical argument
about time travel.

00:16:28.530 --> 00:16:30.130
Maybe this aspect of the story,

00:16:30.130 --> 00:16:33.090
as trippy and sometimes
nonsensical as it is,

00:16:33.090 --> 00:16:35.310
is in service of a larger message.

00:16:35.310 --> 00:16:37.820
We're brought back to
the idea of metaphor.

00:16:37.820 --> 00:16:39.830
The beginning of Legions final episode.

00:16:39.830 --> 00:16:42.350
Starts with this text
flashing across the screen.

00:16:42.350 --> 00:16:45.280
This is the end, the beginning, the end.

00:16:45.280 --> 00:16:47.350
what it all means is not for us to know.

00:16:47.350 --> 00:16:49.040
It is for history to decide.

00:16:49.040 --> 00:16:51.580
All we can do is play
the parts as written.

00:16:51.580 --> 00:16:53.610
All we can know is ourselves.

00:16:53.610 --> 00:16:54.443
On the surface of it

00:16:54.443 --> 00:16:56.030
it seems strange for Legion

00:16:56.030 --> 00:16:57.940
to frame the final episode with a quote.

00:16:57.940 --> 00:17:01.030
After all if David and company
are just playing their parts

00:17:01.030 --> 00:17:03.730
as written, how are they
supposed to change the past?

00:17:03.730 --> 00:17:04.880
And what does self knowledge

00:17:04.880 --> 00:17:07.230
have to do with, well, anything?

00:17:07.230 --> 00:17:09.770
But what if this text is a metaphor?

00:17:09.770 --> 00:17:12.090
Asking us to reframe everything we've seen

00:17:12.090 --> 00:17:14.830
in three seasons,
according to these words.

00:17:14.830 --> 00:17:18.160
In this case, the show hints
that everything David has done,

00:17:18.160 --> 00:17:20.000
past and present from being born,

00:17:20.000 --> 00:17:21.850
to cartoon fighting Amhal Farouk,

00:17:21.850 --> 00:17:23.070
has been necessary.

00:17:23.070 --> 00:17:26.200
That David needed to quiet
literally experience time

00:17:26.200 --> 00:17:30.050
in order for him to change,
and thereby save the world.

00:17:30.050 --> 00:17:32.590
And while it might seem
like we're reaching here,

00:17:32.590 --> 00:17:35.010
this theory does fit with
the rest of the show.

00:17:35.010 --> 00:17:36.770
In fact the idea that characters

00:17:36.770 --> 00:17:38.890
needed to experience time to change,

00:17:38.890 --> 00:17:41.760
is integral to all our major players art.

00:17:41.760 --> 00:17:44.560
Syd for example must
live a second childhood

00:17:44.560 --> 00:17:45.730
in the astral plane,

00:17:45.730 --> 00:17:47.310
under the watch of Oliver and Melanie.

00:17:47.310 --> 00:17:50.400
She goes from the
understandably rage-filled girl

00:17:50.400 --> 00:17:54.120
shooting her rapist, to a
kickass self actualized woman

00:17:54.120 --> 00:17:55.720
who knows how to save the world.

00:17:56.630 --> 00:17:57.503
- I know honey.

00:17:59.930 --> 00:18:00.980
But here's the thing,

00:18:03.340 --> 00:18:04.763
the real world needs you.

00:18:07.210 --> 00:18:10.223
All those bad things,
they don't have to be bad.

00:18:11.870 --> 00:18:12.980
They can be fixed.

00:18:12.980 --> 00:18:15.870
- Likewise, the 30 plus
years Amhal Farouk spent

00:18:15.870 --> 00:18:17.829
in Davids head has changed him.

00:18:17.829 --> 00:18:21.563
- I saw what he saw, I felt what he felt,

00:18:23.029 --> 00:18:25.393
I thought what he thought.

00:18:26.740 --> 00:18:30.870
And over time, what was once
a prison became a person.

00:18:30.870 --> 00:18:31.970
- [Michael] When present Farouk

00:18:31.970 --> 00:18:34.060
finally sizes up his past self,

00:18:34.060 --> 00:18:35.840
he can barely contain the contempt

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:37.839
for the person he once was.

00:18:37.839 --> 00:18:39.100
(foreign language)

00:18:39.100 --> 00:18:41.153
- You have become soft in your old age.

00:18:42.000 --> 00:18:45.233
Was I really this miserable
and filled with hate?

00:18:46.691 --> 00:18:47.927
How petty you seem.

00:18:47.927 --> 00:18:51.130
- [Michael] But what about
David, does he really change?

00:18:51.130 --> 00:18:52.560
According to our girl Syd,

00:18:52.560 --> 00:18:54.810
there's no saving the present David.

00:18:54.810 --> 00:18:56.210
He's broken goods.

00:18:56.210 --> 00:18:59.670
- David, adult David, we can't save him,

00:18:59.670 --> 00:19:01.480
he's too far gone.

00:19:01.480 --> 00:19:06.480
But a baby, this baby, him we can save.

00:19:07.170 --> 00:19:09.410
- [Michael] So how does
time help David change?

00:19:09.410 --> 00:19:12.620
Quite literally by
unwriting his existence.

00:19:12.620 --> 00:19:14.850
Listen to this narration
David gives in the beginning

00:19:14.850 --> 00:19:15.890
of the final episode.

00:19:15.890 --> 00:19:18.680
Again it serves to reframe
everything we've seen

00:19:18.680 --> 00:19:19.970
up to this point in the show.

00:19:19.970 --> 00:19:23.573
- [Narrator] Lessons in
time travel, chapter zero.

00:19:24.870 --> 00:19:27.683
Who we were does not
dictate who we will be.

00:19:29.410 --> 00:19:32.573
But often, it's a pretty good indication.

00:19:41.080 --> 00:19:42.790
Time travel does not give one

00:19:42.790 --> 00:19:45.393
the opportunity to change ones self.

00:19:46.520 --> 00:19:49.710
But rather to eradicate ones self.

00:19:57.820 --> 00:20:00.190
And allow something
else to form in the wake

00:20:00.190 --> 00:20:01.670
of what once was.

00:20:01.670 --> 00:20:03.930
- [Michael] In other
words, change for David

00:20:03.930 --> 00:20:06.150
could only come through destruction.

00:20:06.150 --> 00:20:07.840
And he could only achieve that destruction

00:20:07.840 --> 00:20:09.600
by messing with time.

00:20:09.600 --> 00:20:11.490
It's madness, and it's a complete twist

00:20:11.490 --> 00:20:13.440
on how other characters experience time

00:20:13.440 --> 00:20:17.020
in order to change, but
madness is David's m.o.

00:20:17.020 --> 00:20:19.270
Finally, in the closing
minutes of the show,

00:20:19.270 --> 00:20:20.610
Legion seems to suggest,

00:20:20.610 --> 00:20:23.450
that there's almost a
cosmic plan to this change.

00:20:23.450 --> 00:20:25.150
Whether it's Sydney's second childhood,

00:20:25.150 --> 00:20:26.780
or David's suicide gamble.

00:20:26.780 --> 00:20:29.160
When Switch dies in the final episode,

00:20:29.160 --> 00:20:30.950
it's revealed that she's not human at all,

00:20:30.950 --> 00:20:34.096
but quite literally the
embodiment of time itself.

00:20:34.096 --> 00:20:34.929
- How do you know?

00:20:34.929 --> 00:20:36.930
- I am time, I see all.

00:20:36.930 --> 00:20:38.350
- [Michael] When Switch
returns back to Earth,

00:20:38.350 --> 00:20:40.470
she lets everyone know
that there was meaning

00:20:40.470 --> 00:20:42.270
to the change they underwent.

00:20:42.270 --> 00:20:44.087
That Switch, as the embodiment of time

00:20:44.087 --> 00:20:47.110
and the universe itself
has validated them.

00:20:47.110 --> 00:20:52.110
- Sydney Barrett, Gabriel
Xavier and the Infant David,

00:20:55.200 --> 00:20:57.393
the universe acknowledges you,

00:20:58.590 --> 00:21:02.443
that you exist, and that
your existence is important.

00:21:03.410 --> 00:21:04.960
I can see that you've suffered.

00:21:06.720 --> 00:21:09.163
That people you love have suffered.

00:21:10.650 --> 00:21:12.900
And you want to know
that it meant something.

00:21:15.240 --> 00:21:18.103
It did, it does.

00:21:19.310 --> 00:21:22.520
Nothing of value is ever lost.

00:21:22.520 --> 00:21:25.100
- And even though the
present them will perish,

00:21:25.100 --> 00:21:27.370
it was also better versions of themselves

00:21:27.370 --> 00:21:29.150
shall flourish in their place.

00:21:29.150 --> 00:21:32.480
So what do we make of Legion's
take on time and change?

00:21:32.480 --> 00:21:33.970
Again, I think it's best to invoke

00:21:33.970 --> 00:21:35.810
Davidson's work on metaphor here.

00:21:35.810 --> 00:21:37.610
As Davidson rightly points out.

00:21:37.610 --> 00:21:39.950
How many facts are
conveyed by a photograph?

00:21:39.950 --> 00:21:43.550
None, an infinity, or one
great unstatable fact?

00:21:43.550 --> 00:21:44.420
Bad question.

00:21:44.420 --> 00:21:46.810
A picture is not worth a thousand words,

00:21:46.810 --> 00:21:47.940
or any other number.

00:21:47.940 --> 00:21:51.230
Words are the wrong currency
to exchange for a picture.

00:21:51.230 --> 00:21:54.390
In the same way, holding
Legion's take on time and change

00:21:54.390 --> 00:21:57.810
to a philosophical standard
might not be the right approach.

00:21:57.810 --> 00:21:58.760
At the end of the day,

00:21:58.760 --> 00:22:00.470
Noah Holley decided to not make

00:22:00.470 --> 00:22:02.410
a philosophical argument with the show,

00:22:02.410 --> 00:22:04.090
but rather an artistic one.

00:22:04.090 --> 00:22:05.340
And like in time travel,

00:22:05.340 --> 00:22:08.210
in this choice there is a
sort of grace or madness.

00:22:08.210 --> 00:22:10.080
Whatever deeper meaning there is here,

00:22:10.080 --> 00:22:12.850
if any at all, this show's
not giving us any hints.

00:22:12.850 --> 00:22:15.690
Overall we give Legion a 5/10 for smarts.

00:22:15.690 --> 00:22:18.290
But hey, maybe we're just not getting it.

00:22:18.290 --> 00:22:20.500
Thanks for watching guys, peace.

00:22:20.500 --> 00:22:23.083
(upbeat music)

